WEBVTT

00:01:01.878 --> 00:01:04.121
Come on, let's say good
night to your brother.

00:01:08.897 --> 00:01:13.153
'Night Sam. Good night, love.

00:01:14.769 --> 00:01:16.154
Hey! Dean.

00:01:16.194 --> 00:01:18.503
Daddy! Hey! Buddy.

00:01:18.599 --> 00:01:21.336
What do you think? Sam is ready
to touch around football yet?

00:01:21.336 --> 00:01:23.200
No, daddy. No?

00:01:23.247 --> 00:01:24.931
You got him? I got him.

00:01:27.412 --> 00:01:29.126
Sweet dreams, Sammy.

00:02:00.456 --> 00:02:01.482
John?

00:02:22.378 --> 00:02:25.176
John, is he hungry?

00:02:27.314 --> 00:02:28.134
Okay.

00:03:09.719 --> 00:03:11.506
Sammy!

00:03:19.017 --> 00:03:19.734
Mary!

00:03:20.882 --> 00:03:21.702
Mary!

00:03:26.483 --> 00:03:27.245
Mary!

00:03:34.969 --> 00:03:36.214
Hey, Sammy.

00:03:37.948 --> 00:03:39.061
Okay?

00:03:56.595 --> 00:03:57.459
Mary!

00:04:11.235 --> 00:04:12.129
Daddy!

00:04:12.222 --> 00:04:13.886
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.300
Don't look back!

00:04:15.486 --> 00:04:16.702
Now, Dean! Go!

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:33.518
It's okay, Sam.

00:04:44.786 --> 00:04:46.834
I got it. I got it.

00:04:50.791 --> 00:04:51.436
Here.

00:05:07.539 --> 00:05:09.576
Stay back. You have to stay back.

00:05:29.456 --> 00:05:29.886
Sam!

00:05:30.458 --> 00:05:32.155
Get a move on, would ya?

00:05:32.156 --> 00:05:34.261
We were supposed to be
there like 15 minutes ago.

00:05:35.282 --> 00:05:37.041
Sam, you coming or what?

00:05:37.633 --> 00:05:41.322
Do I have to? Yes. It'll be fun.

00:05:42.306 --> 00:05:44.051
And where's your costume?

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:49.059
You know how I feel about Halloween.

00:05:55.515 --> 00:05:58.376
So here's to Sam and his
awesome LSAT* victory.

00:05:58.483 --> 00:05:59.956
All right, all right.
It's not that big a deal.

00:05:59.957 --> 00:06:02.568
Yeah, he acts all humble,
but he scored a 174.

00:06:03.834 --> 00:06:06.073
Is that good? Scary good.

00:06:06.115 --> 00:06:08.441
See, there you go. You are
a first-Round draft pick.

00:06:08.956 --> 00:06:10.812
You can go to any law school you want.

00:06:10.813 --> 00:06:13.082
Actually, I got an
interview here monday.

00:06:13.551 --> 00:06:16.706
If it goes okay, I think I got
a shot at a full ride next year.

00:06:16.747 --> 00:06:18.636
Hey, it's gonna go great.

00:06:20.048 --> 00:06:20.773
It better.

00:06:20.805 --> 00:06:23.216
How does it feel to be the
golden boy in your family?

00:06:23.222 --> 00:06:24.281
They don't know.

00:06:24.314 --> 00:06:27.111
No? I would be gloating. Why not?

00:06:27.161 --> 00:06:29.185
'Cause we're not exactly the Bradys

00:06:29.237 --> 00:06:31.588
I'm not exactly the
Huxtables. More shots?

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.381
No. No. No. No!

00:06:33.411 --> 00:06:37.460
Seriously, I'm proud of you, and
you're gonna knock them dead on monday.

00:06:37.461 --> 00:06:38.882
You're gonna get that full ride.

00:06:39.245 --> 00:06:40.249
I know it.

00:06:41.086 --> 00:06:42.472
What would I do without you?

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:43.968
Crash and burn.

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:47.957
Whoa! Easy, tiger.

00:07:48.578 --> 00:07:49.383
Dean?

00:07:51.008 --> 00:07:52.471
You scared the crap out of me.

00:07:52.471 --> 00:07:53.921
That's cause you're out of practice.

00:07:56.293 --> 00:07:57.289
Or not.

00:07:57.801 --> 00:07:58.941
Get off of me.

00:07:59.206 --> 00:08:00.975
Dean, what the hell are you doing here?

00:08:01.007 --> 00:08:03.182
I was looking for a beer.

00:08:03.699 --> 00:08:05.536
What the hell are you doing here?

00:08:05.636 --> 00:08:07.341
Ok, all right, we got to talk.

00:08:08.386 --> 00:08:10.900
The phone? If I'd called
would you picked up?

00:08:11.426 --> 00:08:12.263
Sam?

00:08:13.601 --> 00:08:15.667
Jess, hey.

00:08:16.994 --> 00:08:19.002
Dean, this is my girlfriend, Jessica.

00:08:19.726 --> 00:08:21.567
Wait. Your brother Dean?

00:08:21.686 --> 00:08:22.858
I love the Smurfs.

00:08:23.428 --> 00:08:27.173
You know, I got to tell you. You are
completely out of my brother's league.

00:08:27.279 --> 00:08:28.732
Just let me put something on.

00:08:28.779 --> 00:08:32.587
No, no. No, I wouldn't
dream of it, seriously.

00:08:33.623 --> 00:08:36.746
Anyway, I got to borrow your boyfriend here,
talk about some private family business, but

00:08:36.747 --> 00:08:37.938
Nice meeting you.

00:08:39.571 --> 00:08:40.549
No.

00:08:42.485 --> 00:08:44.586
No, whatever you want to say,
you can say it in front of her.

00:08:45.187 --> 00:08:46.190
Okay.

00:08:47.738 --> 00:08:49.723
Dad hasn't been home in a few days.

00:08:50.692 --> 00:08:54.986
So? He's working overtime on a "Miller Time"
shift. He'll stumble back in sooner or later.

00:08:56.002 --> 00:08:58.520
Dad's on a hunting trip,

00:08:58.521 --> 00:09:00.942
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:09:05.874 --> 00:09:07.034
Jess, excuse us.

00:09:08.375 --> 00:09:10.642
We have to go outside.

00:09:10.868 --> 00:09:15.555
I mean, come on, you can't just break in the middle
of the night and expect me to hit the road with you.

00:09:15.556 --> 00:09:17.641
You're not hearing me,
Sammy. Dad's missing.

00:09:17.656 --> 00:09:19.465
I need you to help me find him.

00:09:19.253 --> 00:09:22.584
You remember the poltergeist in
Amherst, or the devil's gates in Clifton?

00:09:22.656 --> 00:09:25.997
He was missing then, too. He's
always missing, and he's always fine.

00:09:25.998 --> 00:09:28.359
Not for this long. Now, are
you gonna come with me or not?

00:09:28.676 --> 00:09:29.649
I'm not.

00:09:30.039 --> 00:09:30.756
Why not?

00:09:30.804 --> 00:09:33.106
I swore I was done hunting. For good.

00:09:33.361 --> 00:09:36.118
Come on, it wasn't easy,
but it wasn't that bad. Yeah?

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:39.935
When I told dad I was scared of the
thing in my closet, he gave me a .45.

00:09:39.967 --> 00:09:41.067
What was he supposed to do?

00:09:41.101 --> 00:09:43.030
I was 9 years old.

00:09:43.759 --> 00:09:46.030
He was supposed to say:
"Don't be afraid of the dark."

00:09:46.088 --> 00:09:47.678
"Don't be afraid of the
dark"? Are you kidding me?

00:09:47.679 --> 00:09:49.836
Of course, you should be afraid.
You know what's out there.

00:09:49.877 --> 00:09:52.533
Yeah I know but still... The way
we grew up after mom was killed

00:09:52.546 --> 00:09:55.096
And dad's obsession to find
the thing that killed her.

00:09:55.141 --> 00:09:57.579
But we still haven't
found the damn thing.

00:09:57.709 --> 00:09:59.255
So we kill everything we can find.

00:09:59.387 --> 00:10:01.689
Save a lot of people doing it, too.

00:10:04.273 --> 00:10:06.026
You think mom would
have wanted this for us?

00:10:08.025 --> 00:10:11.779
The weapon training and
melting the silver into bullets?

00:10:11.856 --> 00:10:14.408
Man, Dean, we were raised like warriors.

00:10:14.434 --> 00:10:15.475
So, what are you gonna do?

00:10:15.675 --> 00:10:18.419
Are you just gonna live
some normal, apple-Pie life?

00:10:18.036 --> 00:10:19.031
Is that it?

00:10:19.168 --> 00:10:21.487
No, not normal. Safe.

00:10:22.015 --> 00:10:23.772
And that's why you ran away.

00:10:27.182 --> 00:10:28.683
I was just going to college.

00:10:28.684 --> 00:10:31.969
It was dad who said if I was
gonna go, I should stay gone.

00:10:33.492 --> 00:10:34.551
And that's what I'm doing.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:38.513
Dad's in real trouble right now if
he's not dead already. I can feel it.

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:42.846
I can't do this alone.

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:44.465
Yes, you can.

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:47.591
Yeah. Well, I don't want to.

00:10:56.037 --> 00:10:57.440
What was he hunting?

00:11:03.343 --> 00:11:06.548
All right. Let's see. Where
the hell did I put that thing?

00:11:06.614 --> 00:11:08.590
So when dad left, why
didn't you go with him?

00:11:08.823 --> 00:11:12.353
I was working my own gig... This
voodoo thing down in New Orleans.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:15.383
Dad let you go on a
hunting trip by yourself?

00:11:15.935 --> 00:11:17.210
I'm 26, dude.

00:11:18.621 --> 00:11:20.350
All right, here we go.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:24.888
So dad was checking out this two-Lane
blacktop just outside of Jericho, California.

00:11:24.987 --> 00:11:26.391
About a month ago, this guy...

00:11:26.656 --> 00:11:29.801
They found his car, but he'd
vanished. Completely M.I.A.

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:32.192
So maybe he was kidnapped.

00:11:32.231 --> 00:11:34.249
Yeah, well, here's another one in April,

00:11:34.393 --> 00:11:39.861
Another one in December '04, '03, '98,
'92... 10 of them over the past 20 years...

00:11:40.156 --> 00:11:42.934
All men, all same
5-Mile stretch of road.

00:11:45.016 --> 00:11:47.103
Started happening more and more, so

00:11:47.136 --> 00:11:48.634
Dad went to go dig around.

00:11:48.656 --> 00:11:50.410
That was about three weeks ago.

00:11:50.815 --> 00:11:53.206
I hadn't heard from him
since, which is bad enough,

00:11:54.446 --> 00:11:56.524
And then I get this
voice mail yesterday.

00:11:57.067 --> 00:12:01.103
<i>Dean, something is starting to
happen. I think it's serious.</i>

00:12:01.191 --> 00:12:03.128
<i>I need to try to figure
out what's going on.</i>

00:12:06.817 --> 00:12:10.078
<i>Be very careful, Dean.
We're all in danger.</i>

00:12:10.746 --> 00:12:12.279
You know there's EVP on that?

00:12:12.377 --> 00:12:15.207
Not bad, Sammy. Kind of
like riding a bike, isn't it?

00:12:15.947 --> 00:12:19.010
All right. I slowed the message
down and ran it through a goldwave,

00:12:19.041 --> 00:12:20.778
Took out the hiss,
and this is what I got.

00:12:22.354 --> 00:12:25.919
<i>I can never go home.</i>

00:12:28.269 --> 00:12:29.865
Never go home.

00:12:35.642 --> 00:12:39.538
You know, in almost two years, I've never
bothered you, never asked you for a thing.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.221
All right, I'll go.

00:12:50.129 --> 00:12:51.615
I'll help you find him,

00:12:51.839 --> 00:12:53.748
But I have to get back
first thing Monday.

00:12:54.108 --> 00:12:55.078
Just wait here.

00:12:55.396 --> 00:12:57.132
What's first thing monday?

00:12:58.607 --> 00:13:00.234
I've this...

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:02.742
I have an interview.

00:13:02.758 --> 00:13:04.567
What? A job interview? Skip it.

00:13:06.374 --> 00:13:10.667
It's a law-School interview, and
it's my whole future on a plate.

00:13:10.739 --> 00:13:11.663
Law school?

00:13:12.543 --> 00:13:14.201
So we got a deal or not?

00:13:18.461 --> 00:13:19.979
Wait, you're taking off?

00:13:20.259 --> 00:13:21.730
Is this about your dad? Is he all right?

00:13:21.871 --> 00:13:24.296
Yeah. You know, just
a little family drama.

00:13:24.769 --> 00:13:27.410
But your brother said he was
on some kind of hunting trip.

00:13:27.465 --> 00:13:30.104
Yeah, he's just deer
hunting up at the cabin,

00:13:30.256 --> 00:13:33.503
And he's probably got Jim,
Jack, and Jose along with him.

00:13:33.506 --> 00:13:35.165
We're just gonna go bring him back.

00:13:35.162 --> 00:13:36.257
What about the interview?

00:13:37.048 --> 00:13:38.206
I'll make the interview.

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:39.750
This is only for a couple days.

00:13:39.856 --> 00:13:42.572
Sam, I mean, please.
Just stop for a second.

00:13:43.514 --> 00:13:44.594
You're sure you're okay?

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:46.570
I'm fine

00:13:47.356 --> 00:13:50.689
It's just... You want
even talk about your family

00:13:51.142 --> 00:13:54.148
And now you're taking off the middle of
the night to spend the week-End with them

00:13:54.367 --> 00:13:57.214
And with Monday coming up...
It's just not kind of your style.

00:13:57.259 --> 00:13:59.570
Hey, everything's gonna be okay.

00:14:00.375 --> 00:14:02.508
I would be back in time, I promise.

00:14:06.224 --> 00:14:07.747
At least tell me where you're going!

00:14:17.819 --> 00:14:19.571
Amy, I can't come over tonight.

00:14:20.543 --> 00:14:23.156
Because I got work in
the morning, that's why.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:27.020
Okay, I miss it, my
dad's gonna have my ass.

00:14:32.634 --> 00:14:34.370
Hey, uh, Amy, let me call you back.

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:49.181
Car trouble or something?

00:14:54.365 --> 00:14:56.399
Take me home.

00:14:57.917 --> 00:14:59.168
Sure, get in.

00:15:15.389 --> 00:15:17.861
So where do you live?

00:15:20.834 --> 00:15:23.400
At the end of Breckenridge Road.

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:27.817
You're coming from a
Halloween party or something?

00:15:31.576 --> 00:15:35.503
You know, um, a girl like you
really shouldn't be alone out here.

00:15:46.813 --> 00:15:48.550
I'm with you.

00:16:00.068 --> 00:16:02.133
Do you think I'm pretty?

00:16:06.936 --> 00:16:08.704
Will you come home with me?

00:16:08.986 --> 00:16:11.770
Um...Hell, yeah.

00:16:31.487 --> 00:16:33.771
Come on. You don't live here.

00:16:35.272 --> 00:16:36.726
I can never go home

00:16:37.086 --> 00:16:41.138
What? What are you talking
about? Nobody lives here.

00:16:41.502 --> 00:16:43.239
Huh, where do you live?

00:16:50.331 --> 00:16:51.974
That's good.

00:16:52.835 --> 00:16:54.290
Joke's over, okay?

00:16:57.652 --> 00:16:59.201
You want me to leave?

00:17:19.028 --> 00:17:19.982
Hello?

00:17:27.421 --> 00:17:28.891
Hello?

00:18:29.627 --> 00:18:31.833
Hey. You want breakfast?

00:18:32.323 --> 00:18:33.434
No, thanks.

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:38.315
So how'd you pay for that stuff? You
and dad still running credit-Card scams?

00:18:38.476 --> 00:18:41.762
Yeah, well, hunting ain't
exactly a pro-Ball career.

00:18:43.326 --> 00:18:45.896
Besides, all we do is apply. It's
not our fault they send us the cards.

00:18:45.927 --> 00:18:50.216
Yeah, and what names did you
write on the application this time?

00:18:50.284 --> 00:18:55.935
Uh... Bert Aframian and his son,
Hector. Scored two cards out of the deal.

00:18:56.029 --> 00:18:57.523
Sounds about right.

00:18:57.540 --> 00:19:00.643
I swear, man,you got to update
your cassette-Tape collection.

00:19:00.715 --> 00:19:01.435
Why?

00:19:01.576 --> 00:19:03.539
Well, for one... They're cassette tapes.

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:04.540
And two...

00:19:04.541 --> 00:19:08.728
Black Sabbath, Motorhead, Metallica?

00:19:09.095 --> 00:19:11.787
It's the greatest hits of mullet rock.

00:19:12.027 --> 00:19:14.321
House rules, Sammy...
driver picks the music,

00:19:14.560 --> 00:19:15.972
Shotgun shuts his cake hole.

00:19:16.739 --> 00:19:19.368
Yo Sammy is a chubby
12-Year-Old. It's...

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:23.154
Sorry, I can't hear you.
The music's too loud.

00:19:39.789 --> 00:19:41.001
Thank you.

00:19:42.211 --> 00:19:45.107
All right. So there's no one matching
dad at the hospital or morgue.

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:46.399
So that's something, I guess.

00:19:49.757 --> 00:19:50.789
Check it out.

00:20:14.488 --> 00:20:15.458
Let's go.

00:20:19.519 --> 00:20:21.272
Did you guys find anything?

00:20:21.303 --> 00:20:23.978
No! Nothing!

00:20:28.865 --> 00:20:32.062
No sign of struggle, no
footprints, no fingerprints...

00:20:32.063 --> 00:20:33.063
Spotless. It's almost too clean.

00:20:33.939 --> 00:20:35.564
So this kid, Troy...

00:20:35.565 --> 00:20:37.563
He's dating your daughter, isn't he? Ya.

00:20:37.564 --> 00:20:38.647
How's Amy doing?

00:20:38.757 --> 00:20:40.806
She's been putting up
missing posters downtown.

00:20:41.901 --> 00:20:44.639
You had another one like
this last month, didn't you?

00:20:45.828 --> 00:20:47.001
And who are you?

00:20:47.549 --> 00:20:48.988
Federal marshals.

00:20:50.526 --> 00:20:52.654
You two are a little young
for marshals, aren't you?

00:20:52.842 --> 00:20:54.500
Thanks, that's awfully kind of you.

00:20:55.068 --> 00:20:56.993
You did have another one
just like this, correct?

00:20:57.149 --> 00:20:57.900
Yeah, that's right,

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:00.419
About a mile up the road. There
have been others before that.

00:21:00.471 --> 00:21:03.178
So this victim... You knew him?

00:21:03.944 --> 00:21:05.931
A town like this,
everybody knows everybody.

00:21:05.994 --> 00:21:08.779
Any connection between the victims
besides that they're all men?

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:10.748
No. Not so far as we can tell.

00:21:11.108 --> 00:21:12.156
So what's the theory?

00:21:12.286 --> 00:21:13.609
Honestly, we don't know...

00:21:13.610 --> 00:21:16.031
Serial murderer, kidnapping ring.

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:20.140
Well, that is exactly the kind of crack
police work I'd expect out of you guys.

00:21:20.598 --> 00:21:22.585
Thank you for your time.

00:21:23.054 --> 00:21:24.822
Gentlemen.

00:21:33.313 --> 00:21:34.328
What was that for?

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:36.955
Why do you have to step on my foot? Why
do you have to talk to police like that?

00:21:37.165 --> 00:21:39.574
Come on. They don't really
know what's going on.

00:21:39.682 --> 00:21:40.842
We're all alone on this.

00:21:40.843 --> 00:21:43.931
If we're gonna find dad, we've got to
get to the bottom of this thing ourselves.

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:47.996
Can I help you boys?

00:21:48.508 --> 00:21:50.308
No, sir. We were just leaving.

00:21:50.309 --> 00:21:52.604
Agent Mulder, agent Scully.

00:22:00.994 --> 00:22:02.324
I'll bet you that's her.

00:22:02.622 --> 00:22:03.529
Yeah.

00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:07.221
You must be Amy. Yeah.

00:22:07.680 --> 00:22:10.574
Troy told us about you. We're his
uncles. I'm Dean. This is Sammy.

00:22:10.809 --> 00:22:12.170
He never mentioned you to me.

00:22:12.749 --> 00:22:13.969
Well, that's Troy, I guess.

00:22:14.016 --> 00:22:15.719
We're not around much.
We're up in Modesto.

00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:19.630
So we're looking for him, too,
and we're kind of asking around.

00:22:19.835 --> 00:22:22.025
Hey, are you okay? Yeah.

00:22:22.265 --> 00:22:24.471
Do you mind if we ask
you a couple questions?

00:22:25.524 --> 00:22:28.210
I was on the phone with
Troy. He was driving home.

00:22:28.211 --> 00:22:33.064
He said he would call me
right back, and he never did.

00:22:33.065 --> 00:22:35.620
He didn't say anything
strange? Or out of the ordinary?

00:22:35.766 --> 00:22:38.613
No, nothing I can remember.

00:22:40.057 --> 00:22:41.403
I like your necklace.

00:22:44.145 --> 00:22:45.381
Troy gave it to me.

00:22:46.028 --> 00:22:49.955
Mostly to scare my parents...
You know, the devil stuff.

00:22:52.431 --> 00:22:54.650
Actually it means just the opposite.

00:22:54.661 --> 00:22:57.398
A pentagram is a
protection against evil.

00:22:57.500 --> 00:23:00.504
Really powerfull, I mean if
you believe in a kind of thing.

00:23:00.649 --> 00:23:02.996
Ok, thank you, Unsolved Mysteries.

00:23:03.246 --> 00:23:04.450
Here's the deal, ladies...

00:23:04.451 --> 00:23:07.954
The way Troy disappeared...
Something's not right.

00:23:07.955 --> 00:23:10.058
So if you've heard anything...

00:23:12.351 --> 00:23:13.259
What is it?

00:23:13.947 --> 00:23:14.877
Well, it's just...

00:23:14.960 --> 00:23:17.906
I mean, with all these guys
going missing, people talk.

00:23:17.952 --> 00:23:19.141
What do they talk about?

00:23:22.916 --> 00:23:25.028
It's kind of this local legend.

00:23:25.294 --> 00:23:29.925
This one girl, she got murdered
out on Centennial like decades ago.

00:23:30.529 --> 00:23:33.173
Well, supposedly, she's still out there.

00:23:33.569 --> 00:23:36.959
She hitchhikes, and
whoever picks her up...

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:40.132
Well, they disappear forever.

00:23:57.232 --> 00:23:59.062
Let me try. I got it.

00:24:00.423 --> 00:24:01.268
Dude.

00:24:02.785 --> 00:24:04.944
You're such a control freak.

00:24:05.679 --> 00:24:08.667
So angry spirits are born out
of violent death, right? Yeah

00:24:09.043 --> 00:24:10.451
Maybe it's not murder.

00:24:18.790 --> 00:24:24.673
This was 1981. Constance Welch, 24 years old,
jumps off Sylvania Bridge, drowns in the river.

00:24:24.704 --> 00:24:26.461
Does it say why she did it? Yeah.

00:24:26.852 --> 00:24:27.415
What?

00:24:28.151 --> 00:24:30.502
An hour before they
found her, she calls 911.

00:24:30.565 --> 00:24:33.716
Her two little kids are in the bathtub.
She leaves them alone for a minute,

00:24:33.717 --> 00:24:34.889
And when she comes back,

00:24:34.961 --> 00:24:36.213
They aren't breathing.

00:24:36.893 --> 00:24:37.910
Both died.

00:24:38.901 --> 00:24:41.488
"Our babies were gone, and
Constance just couldn't bear it,"

00:24:41.489 --> 00:24:42.489
Said husband, Joseph Welch.

00:24:44.867 --> 00:24:46.964
That bridge look familiar to you?

00:24:51.959 --> 00:24:54.963
So this is where Constance
took the swan dive.

00:24:55.260 --> 00:24:57.111
So you think dad would have been here?

00:24:57.893 --> 00:25:00.615
Well, he's chasing the same
story, and we're chasing him.

00:25:02.028 --> 00:25:03.374
Okay, so now what?

00:25:04.359 --> 00:25:06.909
Now we keep digging till we
find him. It might take a while.

00:25:07.107 --> 00:25:10.721
Dean, I told you I've got
to get back by... Monday.

00:25:11.863 --> 00:25:13.631
Right. The interview.

00:25:13.678 --> 00:25:15.258
Yeah. Yeah, I forgot.

00:25:15.921 --> 00:25:17.767
You're really serious
about this, aren't you?

00:25:18.768 --> 00:25:20.974
You think you're just
gonna become some lawyer,

00:25:21.350 --> 00:25:22.601
Marry your girl?

00:25:22.664 --> 00:25:23.806
Maybe. Why not?

00:25:24.014 --> 00:25:27.394
Does Jessica know the truth about you?
Does she know about the things you've done?

00:25:27.597 --> 00:25:29.365
No, and she's not ever going to know.

00:25:30.210 --> 00:25:31.602
Well, that's healthy.

00:25:31.904 --> 00:25:36.425
You can pretend all you want, Sammy, but sooner or
later you're gonna have to face up to who you really are.

00:25:36.852 --> 00:25:37.611
Who is that?

00:25:37.620 --> 00:25:39.117
One of us. No!

00:25:39.246 --> 00:25:41.787
I'm not like you. This is
not going to be my life.

00:25:41.810 --> 00:25:44.878
Well, you have a responsibility. To dad?

00:25:44.206 --> 00:25:45.911
And his crusade?

00:25:46.286 --> 00:25:49.337
If it weren't for pictures, I
wouldn't even know what mom looks like.

00:25:49.732 --> 00:25:51.109
What difference would it make?

00:25:51.359 --> 00:25:53.503
Even if we do find the
thing that killed her,

00:25:54.301 --> 00:25:57.086
Mom's gone, and she isn't coming back.

00:26:03.329 --> 00:26:05.675
Don't talk about her like that.

00:26:14.872 --> 00:26:15.795
Sam.

00:26:28.621 --> 00:26:30.420
Where'd she go? I don't know.

00:26:34.779 --> 00:26:38.424
What the...? Who's driving your car?

00:26:46.108 --> 00:26:48.955
Come on, Dean. Let's go! Go!

00:27:15.356 --> 00:27:16.216
Dean!

00:27:17.637 --> 00:27:18.310
Dean!

00:27:21.134 --> 00:27:21.979
What?!

00:27:25.745 --> 00:27:27.920
Hey, are you all right?

00:27:28.859 --> 00:27:30.032
I'm super.

00:27:35.740 --> 00:27:37.054
Car all right?

00:27:37.257 --> 00:27:39.854
Yeah, whatever she did to
it, it seems all right now.

00:27:40.089 --> 00:27:42.233
That Constance chick... What a bitch!

00:27:42.467 --> 00:27:45.236
Well, she doesn't want us
digging around, that's for sure.

00:27:47.197 --> 00:27:49.481
So where's the trail
go from here, genius?

00:27:54.973 --> 00:27:56.553
You smell like a toilet.

00:27:59.565 --> 00:28:00.785
One room, please.

00:28:04.649 --> 00:28:06.543
You guys having a reunion or something?

00:28:06.840 --> 00:28:07.513
What do you mean?

00:28:07.846 --> 00:28:12.273
That other guy, Bert Aframian. He came in
and bought out a room for the whole month.

00:28:42.939 --> 00:28:45.500
I don't think he's been here
for a couple days at least.

00:28:47.664 --> 00:28:50.323
Salt, cat's-Eye shells...

00:28:50.746 --> 00:28:54.506
He was worried, trying to
keep something from coming in.

00:28:57.525 --> 00:28:58.636
What do you got here?

00:28:59.104 --> 00:29:01.717
Centennial Highway victims.

00:29:03.266 --> 00:29:04.596
I don't get it.

00:29:05.159 --> 00:29:09.070
I mean, different men,
different jobs, age, ethnicities.

00:29:09.780 --> 00:29:11.548
There's always a connection, right?

00:29:12.377 --> 00:29:13.801
What do these guys have in common?

00:29:28.930 --> 00:29:30.260
Dad figured it out.

00:29:30.529 --> 00:29:31.781
What do you mean?

00:29:31.829 --> 00:29:33.898
He found the same article we did.

00:29:33.899 --> 00:29:37.313
Constance Welch. She's a woman in white.

00:29:40.288 --> 00:29:41.774
You sly dogs.

00:29:42.071 --> 00:29:45.435
All right, so if we're dealing with a woman in white,
dad would have found the corpse and destroyed it.

00:29:45.623 --> 00:29:47.219
She might have another weakness.

00:29:47.743 --> 00:29:50.270
No, dad would want to
make sure. He'd dig her up.

00:29:50.329 --> 00:29:51.693
Does it say where she's buried?

00:29:52.117 --> 00:29:53.916
No, not that I can tell.

00:29:54.433 --> 00:29:56.639
If I were dad, though,
I'd go ask her husband,

00:29:57.061 --> 00:29:58.313
If he's still alive.

00:30:04.882 --> 00:30:08.027
All right, why don't you see if you can
find an address? I'm gonna get cleaned up.

00:30:08.469 --> 00:30:13.366
Hey, Dean, what I said earlier
about mom and dad... I'm sorry.

00:30:14.195 --> 00:30:15.618
No chick-Flick moments.

00:30:16.797 --> 00:30:18.596
All right... jerk.

00:30:19.738 --> 00:30:20.614
Bitch.

00:30:37.936 --> 00:30:41.362
<i>Hey, it's me. It's about 10:20...</i>

00:30:41.878 --> 00:30:46.077
Hey, man. I'm starving. I'm gonna grab a little
something to eat at that diner down the street.

00:30:46.078 --> 00:30:47.386
You want anything?

00:30:47.693 --> 00:30:48.262
No.

00:30:48.262 --> 00:30:49.559
Aframian's buying.

00:31:07.055 --> 00:31:09.590
<i>So come home soon, okay? I love you.</i>

00:31:12.453 --> 00:31:12.985
What?

00:31:13.224 --> 00:31:14.554
Dude, five-O. Take off.

00:31:15.023 --> 00:31:16.040
What about you?

00:31:16.306 --> 00:31:18.903
Uh, they kind of
spotted me. Go find dad.

00:31:20.875 --> 00:31:22.064
Problem, officers?

00:31:22.236 --> 00:31:23.487
Where's your partner?

00:31:23.736 --> 00:31:25.786
Partner? What? What partner?

00:31:33.227 --> 00:31:36.825
So fake U.S. Marshal, fake credit cards.

00:31:37.091 --> 00:31:38.546
You got anything that's real?

00:31:39.094 --> 00:31:40.001
My boobs.

00:31:41.933 --> 00:31:44.076
You have the right to remain silent.

00:31:46.382 --> 00:31:48.572
So you want to give us your real name?

00:31:48.922 --> 00:31:52.176
I told you. It's Nugent, Ted Nugent.

00:31:54.366 --> 00:31:57.370
I'm not sure you realize just
how much trouble you're in here.

00:31:57.371 --> 00:32:01.724
We're talking, like, misdemeanor kind of
trouble or "squeal like a pig" trouble?

00:32:02.084 --> 00:32:04.838
You got the faces of 10 missing
persons taped to your wall,

00:32:05.250 --> 00:32:08.160
Along with a whole lot
of satanic mumbo jumbo.

00:32:08.535 --> 00:32:10.475
Boy, you are officially a suspect.

00:32:10.637 --> 00:32:14.611
That makes sense 'cause when the
first one went missing in '82, I was 3.

00:32:15.158 --> 00:32:18.068
I know you got partners.
One of them's an older guy.

00:32:18.851 --> 00:32:20.822
Maybe he started the whole thing.

00:32:22.501 --> 00:32:24.707
So tell me, Dean...

00:32:27.106 --> 00:32:28.029
Is this his?

00:32:35.606 --> 00:32:37.108
I thought that might be your name.

00:32:38.735 --> 00:32:40.281
See, I leafed through this,

00:32:40.295 --> 00:32:43.872
What little I could make out. I
mean, it's nine kinds of crazy,

00:32:45.472 --> 00:32:47.193
But I found this, too.

00:32:48.269 --> 00:32:53.964
Now, you're staying right here till you
tell me exactly what the hell that means.

00:33:06.257 --> 00:33:09.386
Hi, uh, are you Joseph Welch? Yeah.

00:33:10.272 --> 00:33:12.013
Yeah, he was older, but that's him.

00:33:12.095 --> 00:33:15.462
He came by three or four days
ago, said he was a reporter.

00:33:15.821 --> 00:33:18.293
That's right. We're
working on a story together.

00:33:19.542 --> 00:33:23.563
Well, I don't know what the hell kind of story
you're working on... the questions he asked me.

00:33:23.641 --> 00:33:25.471
About your late wife, Constance.

00:33:26.441 --> 00:33:28.178
He asked me where she was buried.

00:33:29.028 --> 00:33:30.639
And where is that again?

00:33:31.249 --> 00:33:32.767
What? I got to go through these twice?

00:33:33.064 --> 00:33:35.409
It's fact checking, if you don't mind.

00:33:38.037 --> 00:33:41.448
In a plot behind my old
place over on Breckenridge.

00:33:42.063 --> 00:33:43.612
Why did you move?

00:33:45.035 --> 00:33:48.477
I'm not gonna live in the
house where my children died.

00:33:51.193 --> 00:33:53.274
Mr. Welch, did you ever marry again?

00:33:53.399 --> 00:33:57.013
No way. Constance... She
was the love of my life,

00:33:58.607 --> 00:34:00.438
Prettiest woman I ever known.

00:34:00.657 --> 00:34:02.096
So you had a happy marriage?

00:34:05.613 --> 00:34:06.411
Definitely.

00:34:09.493 --> 00:34:12.215
Well, that should do
it. Thanks for your time.

00:34:22.801 --> 00:34:25.639
Mr. Welch, you ever
hear of a woman in white?

00:34:25.821 --> 00:34:26.556
A what?

00:34:27.025 --> 00:34:30.170
A woman in white or
sometimes a weeping woman.

00:34:31.207 --> 00:34:32.193
It's a ghost story.

00:34:32.416 --> 00:34:35.718
Well, it's more of a phenomenon, really.

00:34:36.020 --> 00:34:39.494
They're spirits. They've been
sighted for hundreds of years,

00:34:39.854 --> 00:34:44.068
Dozens of places in Hawaii and
Mexico, lately in Arizona, Indiana.

00:34:44.109 --> 00:34:45.987
All these are different
women, you understand,

00:34:46.273 --> 00:34:48.150
But all share the same story.

00:34:49.089 --> 00:34:52.254
Boy, I don't care much for nonsense.

00:34:52.411 --> 00:34:53.772
You see, when they were alive,

00:34:54.215 --> 00:34:56.249
Their husbands were unfaithful to them,

00:34:57.156 --> 00:34:58.236
And these women,

00:34:58.596 --> 00:35:01.662
Basically suffering from temporary
insanity, murdered their children.

00:35:03.332 --> 00:35:06.680
Then, once they realized what they
had done, they took their own lives.

00:35:06.977 --> 00:35:08.729
So now their spirits are cursed,

00:35:09.058 --> 00:35:11.076
Walking back roads, waterways,

00:35:11.410 --> 00:35:14.476
And if they find an
unfaithful man, they kill him,

00:35:14.914 --> 00:35:16.651
And that man is never seen again.

00:35:18.294 --> 00:35:19.764
You think...

00:35:20.921 --> 00:35:24.614
You think that has something
to do with Constance,

00:35:25.240 --> 00:35:26.413
You smart ass?

00:35:27.007 --> 00:35:28.149
You tell me.

00:35:31.574 --> 00:35:36.048
I mean, maybe... Maybe
I made some mistakes,

00:35:36.627 --> 00:35:38.301
But no matter what I did,

00:35:38.990 --> 00:35:41.728
Constance never would have
killed her own children.

00:35:43.156 --> 00:35:45.253
Now, you get the hell out of here,

00:35:45.691 --> 00:35:47.302
And you don't come back.

00:36:02.779 --> 00:36:04.750
I don't know how many
times I got to tell you.

00:36:04.969 --> 00:36:06.581
It's my high-School locker combo.

00:36:07.008 --> 00:36:08.698
Are we gonna do this all night long?

00:36:08.776 --> 00:36:11.858
We just got a 911. Shots
fired over at Whiteford Road.

00:36:13.814 --> 00:36:15.331
Do you have to go to the bathroom?

00:36:15.962 --> 00:36:16.604
No.

00:36:16.932 --> 00:36:17.996
Good.

00:37:07.987 --> 00:37:11.179
Fake 911 phone call, Sammy?
That's pretty illegal.

00:37:11.460 --> 00:37:12.227
You're welcome.

00:37:12.321 --> 00:37:13.604
Listen, we got to talk

00:37:13.697 --> 00:37:16.440
Tell me about it. So the
husband was unfaithful.

00:37:16.534 --> 00:37:18.223
We are dealing with a woman in white.

00:37:18.301 --> 00:37:20.874
She's buried behind her old house.

00:37:20.895 --> 00:37:22.095
Sammy, would you shut up for a second?

00:37:22.139 --> 00:37:24.267
I can't figure out why he
hasn't destroyed the corpse yet.

00:37:24.470 --> 00:37:26.911
That's what I'm trying
to tell you. He's gone.

00:37:27.307 --> 00:37:28.386
Dad left Jericho.

00:37:28.433 --> 00:37:30.279
What? How do you know?

00:37:31.093 --> 00:37:31.906
I've got his journal.

00:37:32.094 --> 00:37:33.705
He doesn't go anywhere
without that thing.

00:37:33.898 --> 00:37:34.993
Well, he did this time.

00:37:35.056 --> 00:37:35.807
What's it say?

00:37:35.838 --> 00:37:38.936
Same old ex-Marine crap when he
wants to let us know where he's going.

00:37:38.999 --> 00:37:39.807
Coordinates.

00:37:39.810 --> 00:37:40.810
Where to?

00:37:40.810 --> 00:37:41.977
I'm not sure yet.

00:37:42.002 --> 00:37:46.100
I don't understand. I mean,
what can be so important

00:37:46.101 --> 00:37:47.101
That he just gets out
in the middle of the job?

00:37:46.717 --> 00:37:48.484
Dean, what the hell is going on?

00:37:51.956 --> 00:37:53.348
Sam, Sam!

00:37:59.757 --> 00:38:01.165
Take me home.

00:38:09.135 --> 00:38:11.341
Take me home.

00:38:13.176 --> 00:38:13.958
No.

00:38:54.811 --> 00:38:56.062
Don't do this.

00:38:58.649 --> 00:39:00.260
I can never go home.

00:39:03.300 --> 00:39:05.130
You're scared to go home.

00:39:12.144 --> 00:39:13.224
Hold me.

00:39:14.303 --> 00:39:16.760
I'm so cold.

00:39:17.171 --> 00:39:21.160
You can't kill me. I'm not unfaithful.

00:39:21.395 --> 00:39:23.194
I've never been.

00:39:24.409 --> 00:39:25.473
You will be.

00:40:10.088 --> 00:40:11.434
I'm taking you home.

00:40:13.905 --> 00:40:14.468
Sam!

00:40:25.554 --> 00:40:27.322
Sam! Here!

00:40:27.369 --> 00:40:28.511
You okay?

00:40:29.199 --> 00:40:30.075
I think.

00:40:30.670 --> 00:40:32.798
Can you move? Yeah. Help me.

00:41:34.177 --> 00:41:36.351
You've come home to us, mommy.

00:42:14.460 --> 00:42:16.431
So this is where she drowned her kids.

00:42:18.105 --> 00:42:19.576
That's why she could never go home.

00:42:21.367 --> 00:42:23.119
She was too scared to face them.

00:42:24.379 --> 00:42:25.959
You found her weak spot.

00:42:26.428 --> 00:42:27.711
Nice work, Sammy.

00:42:30.297 --> 00:42:32.441
I wish I could say the same for you.

00:42:32.566 --> 00:42:34.859
What were you thinking shooting
Casper in the face, you freak?

00:42:34.964 --> 00:42:37.468
Hey, saved your ass.

00:42:38.359 --> 00:42:41.379
I'll tell you another thing.
If you screwed up my car,

00:42:42.942 --> 00:42:44.162
I'll kill you.

00:42:56.735 --> 00:42:59.973
Okay, here's where dad went. It's
called Blackbottle Ridge, Colorado.

00:43:01.209 --> 00:43:02.977
Sounds charming. How far?

00:43:03.191 --> 00:43:05.052
About 600 miles.

00:43:05.756 --> 00:43:08.087
If we shag ass, we
can make it by morning.

00:43:09.976 --> 00:43:11.540
Dean, um...

00:43:14.122 --> 00:43:15.154
You're not going.

00:43:15.295 --> 00:43:17.720
The interview's in 10
hours. I got to be there.

00:43:22.536 --> 00:43:26.651
Yeah. Yeah, whatever.
I'll take you home.

00:43:47.244 --> 00:43:48.731
You'll call me if you find him?

00:43:51.739 --> 00:43:53.476
Maybe I can meet up with you later, huh?

00:43:53.773 --> 00:43:54.633
Yeah, all right.

00:43:58.635 --> 00:43:59.417
Sam.

00:44:03.485 --> 00:44:05.237
You know, we made a hell
of a team back there.

00:44:06.479 --> 00:44:07.073
Yeah.

00:44:26.328 --> 00:44:27.204
Jess!

00:44:29.082 --> 00:44:30.208
You home!?

00:45:12.347 --> 00:45:13.286
No!

00:45:16.232 --> 00:45:17.202
Sam!

00:45:17.233 --> 00:45:18.000
Jess!

00:45:19.752 --> 00:45:21.270
Sam! Sam!

00:45:22.521 --> 00:45:24.320
No! No!

00:45:25.237 --> 00:45:27.991
Jess! Jess! No!

00:46:13.992 --> 00:46:15.713
We got work to do.



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
